  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the simplest estimate is <strong>220 &minus; age</strong>, but the more accurate <strong>Tanaka formula is 208 &minus; 0.7 &times; age</strong>. At 40, that is about <strong>180 bpm</strong>. Individual maximums vary by about &plusmn;10 bpm.</p></div>

